    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0568" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv02/pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72119/3526</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1918-12-30">December 30,
                            1918</date>.<lb/>[Received January 25, 1919.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to Mr. Laughlin’s despatch
                    No. 10265 of the 6th instant,<anchor n="28" xml:id="d421-f1"/> relative to the
                    recognition of the Lettish National Council, I have the honor to transmit
                    herewith, a copy of the original, with translation, of a letter dated the 20th
                    instant, addressed to me by Mr. Henri Simson, containing a protest against the
                    alleged violation by Germany of Article XII of the Armistice, signed on November
                    11 and renewed on December 13, 1918.</p>
                <p>The writer states that the German forces are evacuating Latvia without having
                    received any order from the Allied Powers, and that they are ravaging the
                    country and supporting the Bolshevik forces.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Davis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d421-a1.xml" xpointer="d421-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
